(3. Choose the correct form of the verbs in this text) Tj
T*
(My granny is 93 and she's come to live with us at our house. We're all pleased because we) Tj
T*
(love having her near us. She's a very independent person and until this year, she \(1\)) Tj
T*
(refused / was refusing to move to the flat on our ground floor. But last month she suddenly) Tj
T*
(\(2\) changed / was changing her mind and I \(3\) asked / would ask her why. She explained that) Tj
T*
(for years, nobody in her village \(4\) would lock / was locking their front doors and the) Tj
T*
(place \(5\) used to feel / would feel safe, but last month \(6\) she met / was meeting a) Tj
T*
(neighbour in the street when she \(7\) was walking / would walk home from the shops and \(8\)) Tj
T*
(heard / was hearing some bad news. Thieves \(9\) were breaking / got used to breaking into) Tj
T*
(people's houses while they \(10\) were sitting / would sit in their back gardens.She \(11\)) Tj
T*
(realised / was realising that she \(12\) wasn't wanting / didn't want to live alone any more.) Tj
T*
(She \(13\) isn't used / didn't use to being in the town yet, but it's not as difficult as she) Tj
T*
(\(14\) was thinking / thought it might be, and she loves seeing us more often.) Tj
T*
(4. Fill in the gaps with a suitable form of be/get used to) Tj
T*
(Rita's very tired this morning. She ______ \(not\) going to bed late.) Tj
T*
(Don't worry about the children: they ______ going to school by bus.) Tj
T*
(My new boss ______ giving orders, not receiving them.) Tj
T*
(She ______ \(not\) drinking very strong coffee and it made her ill.) Tj
T*
(______ \(you\) our climate or do you still miss the sunshine?) Tj
T*
(I had never stayed in such an expensive hotel before, but I soon ______ it.) Tj
T*
(5. Complete with Past Simple or Past Continuous) Tj
T*
(Don't ask me about the concert! I ______ \(work\) in the stadium café when the band ______) Tj
T*
(\(play\).) Tj
T*
(I ______ \(look\) round the palace when a man ______ \(stop\) me to ask for directions.) Tj
T*
(The lights ______ \(go\) out while she ______ \(have\) a party in her house.) Tj
T*
(She ______ \(go\) quietly out of her bedroom and ______ \(stand\) behind the door so she could) Tj
T*
