T*
(DESPITE VS IN SPITE OF) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Despite vs. In Spite Of: diferencias y ejercicios · Easy EnglishGRAMMAR · B1-B2Despite vs.) Tj
T*
(In Spite Of: diferencias y ejercicios) Tj
T*
(Cuándo usar despite, in spite of, although y por qué despite of es incorrecto, con) Tj
T*
(transformaciones de Cambridge B2.) Tj
T*
(9 de octubre de 2026) Tj
T*
(Despite e in spite of significan «a pesar de». Despite of es incorrecto. La diferencia) Tj
T*
(principal es de estructura, no de significado.) Tj
T*
(Correcto | Incorrecto |) Tj
T*
(Despite the rain | Despite of the rain |) Tj
T*
(In spite of the rain | Inspite of the rain |) Tj
T*
(Despite being tired | Despite of being tired |) Tj
T*
(1. Seguidos de sustantivo) Tj
T*
(Despite the rain, we went for a walk.A pesar de la lluvia, salimos a pasear.) Tj
T*
(In spite of her problems, she remained optimistic.A pesar de sus problemas, siguió siendo) Tj
T*
(optimista.) Tj
T*
(2. Seguidos de -ing) Tj
T*
(Despite feeling tired, I went to work.A pesar de estar cansado, fui a trabajar.) Tj
T*
(In spite of studying hard, he failed the exam.A pesar de estudiar mucho, suspendió el) Tj
T*
(examen.) Tj
T*
(3. Oración completa: the fact that) Tj
T*
(Utiliza despite the fact that o in spite of the fact that antes de sujeto + verbo.) Tj
T*
(Despite the fact that it was raining, we went outside.A pesar de que llovía, salimos.) Tj
T*
(4. Although vs. despite) Tj
T*
(Although + oración | Despite / in spite of + nombre o -ing |) Tj
T*
(Although he was tired | Despite being tired |) Tj
T*
(Although it was raining | Despite the rain |) Tj
T*
(Although she was nervous | In spite of being nervous |) Tj
T*
(5. Errores frecuentes) Tj
T*
(? Despite of the rain ? ? Despite the rain) Tj
T*
(? Despite she was ill ? ? Despite being ill / Despite the fact that she was ill) Tj
T*
(? In spite of he was tired ? ? In spite of being tired.) Tj
T*
(6. Transformaciones B2) Tj
T*
(Although it was cold, we went swimming. \(DESPITE\)) Tj
T*
(Although she was nervous, she gave a speech. \(IN SPITE OF\)) Tj
T*
(Despite the rain, they played tennis. \(ALTHOUGH\)) Tj
T*
(He passed the exam although he hadn't studied much. \(DESPITE\)) Tj
T*
(Mostrar solucionesDespite the cold, we went swimming.) Tj
T*
(In spite of being nervous, she gave a speech.) Tj
T*
(Although it was raining, they played tennis.) Tj
T*
(Despite not having studied much, he passed the exam.) Tj
T*
(Fuentes de consulta: Cambridge Dictionary y British Council.) Tj
T*
(Sigue aprendiendo: Conectores de contraste · Despite / In spite of · Police Vocabulary ·) Tj
T*
(Past Tenses: ejercicios resueltos) Tj
T*
ET
